CytoTrack AI research-use notice
================================

CytoTrack AI source code is released under the MIT License. Research outputs
should cite this software and every source dataset/model listed in the result
folder provenance.

Default result path
-------------------

The default detector/tracking path uses the local classical multi-strategy
detector, centroid-based tracking, self-repair quality checks, and locally
generated plots/dashboards. This path avoids optional non-commercial model
backends.

Optional components with extra restrictions
-------------------------------------------

NVIDIA LocateAnything-3B is optional and opt-in. It is not installed by default
and is not used by the default research-paper result path. If a run uses it,
the run manifest must say so and the user must comply with the NVIDIA model
license.

LIVECell images/annotations are not redistributed by this repository. If a
user separately trains with LIVECell, the resulting paper must cite LIVECell
and respect the LIVECell CC BY-NC 4.0 data/model license.

PyQt5 is an open-source GPL/commercial Qt binding. Source-code use in this
repository remains MIT, but distributing a binary that includes PyQt5 requires
GPL-compliant distribution or a commercial PyQt license. For simplest binary
redistribution under permissive terms, migrate the GUI binding to an LGPL Qt
binding such as PySide6 or use the non-Qt result-generation scripts.

Result bundle rule
------------------

Every paper-facing result folder should contain:

- videos or dashboard media used for inspection,
- CSV tables for tracks and migration measurements,
- plots and interactive dashboards,
- manifest/provenance with software version, detector backend, source movie,
  training inputs, dataset licenses, and citation obligations,
- QC/audit files showing coverage and identity checks.
